{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "deckard",
  "name": "Deckard",
  "role": "Healer",
  "overview": "Deckard is a Healer specialized in single-target healing, with the possibility to prepare Healing Potion on the ground for later usage, and crowd control, usually used as follow-up to your Tank's engage.",
  "strengths": [
    "Strong and efficient single-target healing output",
    "Powerful area of effect crowd control",
    "Access to Emerald for healing reduction"
  ],
  "weaknesses": [
    "Weak against burst damage",
    "No access to Cleanse or similar tools to remove crowd-control effects",
    "Struggles when facing high-mobility Heroes",
    "Unable to provide Unstoppable frames"
  ],
  "synergies": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "johanna",
        "name": "Johanna"
      },
      {
        "id": "blaze",
        "name": "Blaze"
      },
      {
        "id": "sgt-hammer",
        "name": "Sgt. Hammer"
      },
      {
        "id": "jaina",
        "name": "Jaina"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Scroll Of Sealing makes Deckard excellent at following up on Heroes that can provide their own source of reliable crowd control (for example Johanna) and similarly good at setting up enemy Heroes for allied skillshot-based Abilities (such as Kel'Thuzad).\n\nHealing Potion is extremely easy to use for healing allied Heroes without mobility, so they are great to have on Deckard's side. For the same reason, you should avoid picking high-mobility Heroes and/or dive Heroes."
  },
  "counters": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "johanna",
        "name": "Johanna"
      },
      {
        "id": "deathwing",
        "name": "Deathwing"
      },
      {
        "id": "tracer",
        "name": "Tracer"
      },
      {
        "id": "li-ming",
        "name": "Li-Ming"
      },
      {
        "id": "malfurion",
        "name": "Malfurion"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "With little in the way of mobility, Deckard struggles against Heroes who can easily engage on him, especially if they are ranged.\n\nHeroes who have access to Unstoppable effects have easy life against Deckard as they can ignore all his offensive Abilities. Similarly, Cleanse effects (for example Intercession by Whitemane) are good against Deckard because they basically deny his main strength: crowd control.\n\nDeckard can make up for his weakness to burst damage by taking short fights, however, the enemy team will usually still have an edge during them."
  },
